<title>INDIA: India's LML 96/97 6-month net higher.</title>
<headline>India's LML 96/97 6-month net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		172.0  vs    81.6</p>
<p>    Gross sales	   3,639.4  vs 2,896.4</p>
<p>    Other income	     18.1  vs    36.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   3,275.7  vs 2,713.2</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   97.1  vs    78.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     69.2  vs    59.6</p>
<p>    Tax			  *     vs    --</p>
<p>    Exceptional item**     43.5  vs    --</p>
<p>Note: * Indian two-wheeler maker LML Limited said a minimum alternate tax of 22 million was being treated as a &quot;tax credit&quot; and would be carried forward to be set off in subsequent years.</p>
<p>** LML said it had written off a sum of 43.5 million rupees as an extraordinary loss arising out of the non-recovery of dues from Esslon Synthetics Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
